POST-QUANTUM READINESS QUESTION #9
CAN YOUR ORGANIZATION UPDATE CRYPTOGRAPHY WITHOUT REWRITING APPLICATIONS?
Most organizations know what cryptography they use. Some know where it is used. But very few can replace cryptographic algorithms quickly.
When quantum-safe migration begins, every application should not require code rewrites.
Ask yourself:
👉 Can you switch from RSA/ECC to PQC without modifying business applications?
👉 Is cryptography centralized or embedded inside application code?
👉 Can new algorithms be deployed across thousands of systems consistently?
👉 Do your applications support cryptographic agility?
👉 Can multiple algorithms run simultaneously during migration?
👉 How long would it take to replace a vulnerable algorithm across your enterprise?
Common Challenges
🔒 Hard-coded cryptographic libraries
🔒 Different encryption implementations across teams
🔒 Legacy applications with outdated algorithms
🔒 No centralized cryptographic policy
🔒 Vendor lock-in
🔒 No testing strategy for hybrid cryptography
Post-Quantum Readiness Requires
✅ Cryptographic Agility
✅ Centralized Crypto Services
✅ Policy-Based Algorithm Management
✅ Hybrid Classical + PQC Support
✅ Automated Algorithm Updates
✅ Standardized Cryptographic APIs
✅ Continuous Compliance Monitoring
The Reality
Organizations that prepare early won't just replace algorithms...
They will build systems capable of adapting to every future cryptographic transition.
Quantum readiness is not about one migration.
It is about building cryptographic agility for decades to come.